            <ArticleTitle>Coronary vasospasm-induced ventricular tachyarrhythmias.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>609-14</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary artery spasm has been shown to play an important role in the pathogenesis of not only variant angina but also various arrhythmias. We present a case report of coronary vasospasm-induced arrhythmia and review the prevalence, mechanism, prognosis and management of this problem.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
